15 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a bathymetric map of the East Sea showing major currents \(EKWC, NKCC, NB, OB\) and geographic features such as Ulleung Island, Dok Island, Korea Strait, and the Ulleung Basin, with color indicating depth. Panel B displays sampling stations as blue diamonds for NIFS and a shaded area for KMA and KIOST, covering part of the East Sea between Korea and Japan.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Panel A contains a schematic workflow for predicting subsurface temperature via a conditional computation model using surface data, including input, feature extraction with MLP and CNN, regression, decision module, and output. Panel B shows eddy structure analysis with depth-wise tilting and three morphology types \(bowl, shallow-expanded lens, deep-lens expanded\) highlighting energy conversion and eddy interactions. Panel C illustrates rotational behavior and state classification using wobbling ratio formulas, showing rotational layers, mathematical definitions, and a phase diagram for growth and decay phases.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Panel A is a map showing underwater eddy trajectories as curved colored lines and eddy centers as open circles off an east Asian coast, using latitude and longitude. Panel B is a horizontal bar chart depicting eddy lifespan in days by year and month from 1993 to 2023, with color intensity representing lifespan duration according to a side color scale, and a highlighted long-lived event from November 2014 to August 2016.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a scatter plot with colored circles representing eddy centers at the surface over time, traced from April 20 to May 25, color-coded by days. Panel B presents a line graph showing azimuthal current speed versus radial profile at different depths, with speeds decreasing as depth increases.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating gyroscopic motion. Panel A shows a tilted spinning cylinder with labeled spin axis, precession axis, angular velocities, and forces. Panel B visualizes precession as a blue dashed path and nutation as a red wavy line.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Panel A maps the full independent test set as blue dots and indicates the Ulleung Basin subset with yellow shading. Panels B and C show depth-dependent RMSE profiles for temperature and salinity. Red dashed lines with stars represent the test set, blue dashed lines with circles represent the full independent test set, and yellow solid lines with circles represent the Ulleung Basin subset. Panels D and E map horizontal temperature and salinity RMSE at selected depths from 10 to 300 m. Panels F and G show the observed time-depth distributions, while Panels H and I show the corresponding CCM-produced temperature and salinity distributions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Four 3D graphs \(A\205D\) display ocean temperature anomalies by depth, latitude, and longitude for four dates in 2015, showing changes from S-lens to bowl structures. Panel E is a line graph comparing radius changes at four depths across dates. Panel F shows a time series of tilt values from March to October 2015, with vertical dashed lines marking the same four dates as above.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Four-panel scientific figure showing time series data from March to October 2015. Panel A plots water volume with annotated peak and trough dates: 18 April, 26 May, 1 July, and 16 September. Panel B shows line plots for EKE \(red\), PEP \(blue\), and ETE \(gray\) with two shaded periods labeled Event 1 and Event 2. Panel C presents BCI \(red\) and BTI \(blue\) values, with shaded periods matching those in Panel B. Panel D displays blue bars for WR values, separated into four periods \(P1\205P4\) with corresponding WR regime values, and a red horizontal line denoting the regime threshold.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Five scatter plots labeled A through E display relationships between Volume and different variables: WR, dEKE/dt, dPEP/dt, BCI, and BTI, each with a regression line and data points colored by density. Panel A shows a strong negative correlation between Volume and WR \(Pearson r = -0.57, p = 1.03e-19\). Panels B and C show weak correlations with dEKE/dt and dPEP/dt, respectively, with Pearson r values close to zero. Panel D shows a moderate positive correlation between Volume and BCI \(Pearson r = 0.26, p = 9.66e-05\). Panel E shows a moderate negative correlation between Volume and BTI \(Pearson r = -0.36, p = 0.52e-08\). Each plot includes a color bar indicating point density.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a precessing top with its axis tilted and rotating in a circular path. Panel B shows an upright top spinning on its vertical axis. Panel C shows a tilted top precessing in the opposite direction with its axis tracing a horizontal circle. Panel D presents a time series line graph from March to October 2015, comparing the geometric component in red and dynamical component in blue, with phase labels P1 to P4 and their respective WR values displayed above the graph.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Panels A-D show the evolution of UWE16 from January to May 2016. Panel A plots eddy volume with red reference points. Panel B plots eddy kinetic energy, perturbation potential energy, and total eddy energy, with Event 3 highlighted. Panel C plots baroclinic and barotropic conversion. Panel D shows the Wobbling Ratio during periods P5-P7. Panel E presents the paired three-dimensional structures of UWE16 and the Dok Cold Eddy on 25 May 2016. Red and blue ellipses outline their respective boundaries, white dots mark the eddy centers, blue dots mark local ADT extrema, and dashed and solid lines indicate the tilt and vertical axes, respectively.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
